[
    ["T1 Menu release", "At Treatment, start an assessment that kneels the medic. Close with ESC during entry and after the hold begins. Repeat with a different patient, a weapon equipped, and while cancelling treatment. Stand, turn and walk without having to reopen the menu."],
    ["T2 Carrier and Semi-Fowler", "At Transfer, use the casualty with a plate carrier and no backpack. Remove the carrier and check its cargo, then restore it. Place the casualty in Semi-Fowler, load the SkedCo, and walk through the old bolster location. Verify face-up alignment and retained kit."],
    ["T3 IV and transfusion", "At Treatment, bandage the bleeding leg, establish IV access on the other limb, prime and run fluid. Confirm amount and flow status. Stop, remove the line, cancel a fresh setup, and reopen the menu. Inspect the provider and patient gear for duplicate or lost supplies."],
    ["T4 HPMK and SkedCo", "If testing Zeus, enable the test curator and place the SkedCo inventory item. Wrap, expose and re-cover the casualty through the medical menu. Load a named casualty from the litter list, then try the hips action on a fresh run. Check HPMK fit, solo drag, two handle claims, free movement, lift and release."],
    ["T5 Talon and evacuation", "Deploy the folded Talon, load the casualty, and check that the lift is offered with three bearers. Carry to the vehicle, load and unload a free seat, then observe the restored litter and unstrap. Fold it empty. Use the optional Hatchet for the seat test if loaded."],
    ["T6 Hardigg inventory", "Open the field-marked chest, inspect lid tape and body marks, and open inventory through vanilla and ACE. Hold Gear open on a second client while the first exits. Drawers should close when the final viewer leaves. Close the lid and repeat with the black lid."],
    ["T7 Ownership and late join", "Have one player opt into the casualty role. Repeat treatment and transport, disconnect a bearer while lifted, and join with a new client while the casualty is packaged. Compare client and server RPT, then release the patient and verify original ACE carry and drag are available."],
    ["T8 Server load", "Compare the 24-AI workloads after warm-up, keeping mods, player count and server settings fixed. Capture the steady window with menus closed. In an independent window, exercise blood stock moves, cooler deployment and casualty treatment. Compare frame times and named timing rows."]
]
